{"id": 3, "ts": 1780577461.5922086, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019d like to start by putting Candidate\u202fB forward as the provisional choice.\u202fHe demonstrates the core reliability and stress\u2011resilience we need for long\u2011distance operations: he is described as \u201cvery conscientious\u201d and \u201chandles stress very well,\u201d which directly supports operational reliability and calmness under pressure.\u202fHis technical competence is also solid \u2013 he \u201cassesses weather conditions\u201d accurately and has \u201cexcellent computer skills,\u201d both critical for complex flight planning and in\u2011flight decision support.\u202fWhile his interpersonal style has some drawbacks \u2013 being seen as pretentious and occasionally using the wrong tone \u2013 these are limited to communication style rather than outright hostility, and can be mitigated through cockpit resource management training.\u202fOverall, his strengths in reliability, stress handling, and technical ability outweigh the relatively minor communication concerns, making him the strongest overall fit at this stage."}
