{"id": 14, "ts": 1780577541.5325704, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I agree with James that Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strong stress resilience, conscientiousness, and solid technical competence are critical for long\u2011distance operations. However, I want to highlight Candidate\u202fC as a noteworthy alternative: he is described as \u201c100\u202f% reliable\u201d and \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d which directly addresses the crew\u2011cooperation concerns we have raised for both B and D. Yet C also \u201chas difficulty communicating ideas,\u201d is \u201cregarded as egocentric,\u201d and \u201cis not very willing to further his education,\u201d which raise serious doubts about his adaptability and feedback orientation\u2014key for safety\u2011critical, evolving environments. Given that B\u2019s communication style, while imperfect, appears less likely to jeopardize cockpit dynamics than C\u2019s egocentricity, I still provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fB, while keeping C as the strongest alternative pending any further evidence on his teamwork impact."}
